  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN209.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷai vaṟpuṟukkun toḻi colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said when comforting HER who had undergone changes in the time of separation. [RK, VP, ER: How the confidante consoled HER.]</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN209.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>tō<supplied>ḷu</supplied>n tolkaviṉ ṟolaintaṉa nāḷu</l>
        <l>maṉṉaiyu maruntuya ruṟṟaṉa ḷalarē </l>
        <l>poṉṉaṇi neṭuntērt teṉṉar kōmā</l>
        <l>ṉeḻuvuṟaḻ <supplied>ti</supplied>ṇitō ḷiyaṟērc ceḻiya</l>
        <l>ṉērā veḻuva raṭippaṭak kaṭanta</l>
        <l>vālaṅ kāṉat tārppiṉum periteṉa</l>
        <l>vāḻal vāḻi tōḻi yavarē</l>
        <l>māal yāṉai maṟappōrp pullik</l>
        <l>kāmpuṭai neṭuvarai vēṅkaṭat tumpa </l>
        <l>raṟaiyiṟan takaṉṟaṉa rāyiṉu niṟaiyiṟan</l>
        <l>tuḷḷā rāka laritē cevvēṉ</l>
        <l>muḷḷūr maṉṉaṉ kaḻaṟoṭik kāri</l>
        <l>cellā nallicai niṟutta valvi</l>
        <l>lōrik koṉṟu cēralark kītta</l>
        <l>cevvērp palaviṉ payaṅkeḻu kolli</l>
        <l>nilaipeṟu kaṭavu <supplied>ḷā</supplied>kkiya</l>
        <l>palarpukaḻ pāvai yaṉṉaniṉ ṉalaṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="6d">Thinking</l>
        <l corresp="1">“[My] shoulders have lost their old beauty, and daily</l>
        <l corresp="2">mother experiences daunting misery. The gossip,</l>
        <l corresp="6a-c">it is louder than the uproar in Ālaṅkāṉam</l>
        <l corresp="3">when the king of the Southerners with a gold-adorned large chariot,</l>
        <l corresp="4">Ceḻiyaṉ with firm shoulders like cross-bars [and] an advancing chariot,</l>
        <l corresp="5">overcame those rising [against him]  in discord, so that they became [his] servants,”</l>
        <l corresp="7">don’t be downcast, oh friend. He,</l>
        <l corresp="10a-c">even though he departed, traversing the rocks</l>
        <l corresp="9">beyond Vēṅkaṭam, the tall mountain [grown] with bamboo</l>
        <l corresp="8 10d">of Pulli of valorous battle with large elephants, going beyond self-control</l>
        <l corresp="11a-c">it will be difficult [for him] to be one who forgets</l>
        <l corresp="17">your beauty, [which is] like the idol praised by many</l>
        <l corresp="16">that is created by the gods to obtain a position</l>
        <l corresp="15">on fertile Kolli, [its] jackfruit trees with red roots,</l>
        <l corresp="14">that was given to the Cēra king after killing Ōri,</l>
        <l corresp="13">with a strong bow who has established imperishable fame,</l>
        <l corresp="11d-12">by Kāri with anklets [and] armlets, king of Muḷḷūr with a red/straight spear.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
